      "slug": "fptr",
      "term": "FPtr",
      "definition": "Front post treble. Yarn over, insert hook from front to back to front around the post of a stitch 2 rows below, and complete the treble. The stitch raises forward off the fabric surface."
    },
    {
      "slug": "turning-chain",
      "term": "Turning chain",
      "definition": "Two chains at the start of dc rows; one chain at the start of FPtr rows."
    },
    {
      "slug": "weaving-in-ends",
      "term": "Weaving in ends",
      "definition": "Threading yarn tails through stitches with the tapestry needle."
    }
