      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "An alpine stitch baby blanket is 75 x 90 cm. Odd rows are plain dc. Even rows alternate dc and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "fptr"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "FPtr"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " stitches, with each FPtr worked into the post of a dc 2 rows below. The front post trebles pull forward to make ridges."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "DK cotton shows the raised ridges clearly. The texture is regular and geometric. Total yardage is around 400 g. Alpine stitch uses slightly more yarn than plain dc because the FPtr stitches wrap around the post below."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
